    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading2",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Psalm 55"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Prayer for the Destruction of the Treacherous."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "For the music director; on stringed instruments. A Maskil of David."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Listen to my prayer, God;",
          "And do not hide Yourself from my pleading."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Give Your attention to me and answer me;",
          "I am restless in my complaint and severely distracted,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Because of the voice of the enemy,",
          "Because of the pressure of the wicked;",
          "For they bring down trouble upon me",
          "And in anger they hold a grudge against me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶My heart is in anguish within me,",
          "And the terrors of death have fallen upon me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Fear and trembling come upon me,",
          "And horror has overwhelmed me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I said, “Oh, that I had wings like a dove!",
          "I would fly away and be at rest."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Behold, I would flee far away,",
          "I would spend my nights in the wilderness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“I would hurry to my place of refuge",
          "From the stormy wind and heavy gale.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶Confuse them, Lord, divide their tongues,",
          "For I have seen violence and strife in the city."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Day and night they go around her upon her walls,",
          "And evil and harm are in her midst."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Destruction is in her midst;",
          "Oppression and deceit do not depart from her streets."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶For it is not an enemy who taunts me,",
          "Then I could endure it;",
          "Nor is it one who hates me who has exalted himself against me,",
          "Then I could hide myself from him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But it is you, a man my equal,",
          "My companion and my confidant;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "We who had sweet fellowship together,",
          "Walked in the house of God among the commotion."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "May death come deceitfully upon them;",
          "May they go down alive to Sheol,",
          "For evil is in their dwelling, in their midst."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶As for me, I shall call upon God,",
          "And the Lord will save me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Evening and morning and at noon, I will complain and moan,",
          "And He will hear my voice."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He will redeem my soul in peace from the battle which is against me,",
          "For they are many who are aggressive toward me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God will hear and humiliate them—",
          "Even the One who sits enthroned from ancient times—"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "With whom there is no change,",
          "And who do not fear God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has put forth his hands against those who were at peace with him;",
          "He has violated his covenant."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His speech was smoother than butter,",
          "But his heart was war;",
          "His words were softer than oil,",
          "Yet they were drawn swords."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "¶Cast your burden upon the Lord and He will sustain you;",
          "He will never allow the righteous to be shaken."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But You, God, will bring them down to the pit of destruction;",
          "Men of bloodshed and deceit will not live out half their days.",
          "But I will trust in You."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
